      "file": "demineralization_plant_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Ion exchange swaps salts for H⁺ and OH⁻",
      "description": "The cation resin exchanges Ca²⁺, Mg²⁺, Na⁺ for H⁺ (water becomes acidic); the degasser blows out the CO₂ formed from bicarbonate; the anion resin exchanges Cl⁻, SO₄²⁻, silica for OH⁻; H⁺ + OH⁻ → H₂O. Resins are regenerated with acid and caustic when exhausted (rising conductivity/silica or sodium slip). Typical outlet < 5–10 µS/cm, silica < ~ 0.1 mg/L.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
